  "id": "Compound::DB00883 - Gene::2982",
  "verbalization": "Isosorbide Dinitrate, a nitrate, is linked to Gucy1a3 through a series of molecular and physiological interactions. The evidence suggests that Isosorbide Dinitrate, as part of the nitrate class, binds to Gucy1a3, which is a G-protein coupled receptor involved in vasodilation. This relationship is further supported by the fact that Nitroglycerin, a nitrate, also binds to Gucy1a3, indicating a shared mechanism of action. The lowest common ancestors in the paths highlight the interconnectedness of nitrate esters and vasodilating agents, reinforcing the role of Gucy1a3 in these processes. The causal relationship between Isosorbide Dinitrate and Rebound Hypertension, as well as Withdrawal Hypertension, further underscores the systemic impact of nitrate action on vascular function. The integration of these pathways suggests that Gucy1a3 serves as a critical mediator in the vasodilatory effects of nitrates, with Isosorbide Dinitrate acting through a shared mechanism with Nitroglycerin.",
